WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:02.461
I create the Deslop settings file at

00:02.461 --> 00:04.622
the root of this project. Keeping it

00:04.622 --> 00:06.783
with the code gives the team the

00:06.783 --> 00:08.944
same starting point. I save the file

00:08.944 --> 00:11.106
here, then use the sidebar to check

00:11.106 --> 00:12.649
the effect of my changes.

00:13.449 --> 00:15.757
I add the archive folder to the

00:15.757 --> 00:18.065
exclusions and save the file. Those files

00:18.065 --> 00:20.373
are skipped when Deslop checks the project.

00:20.373 --> 00:22.681
Hiding a reported file is a different

00:22.681 --> 00:24.989
choice: it changes what I see in

00:24.989 --> 00:27.297
the results while the file is still

00:27.297 --> 00:27.627
checked.

00:28.427 --> 00:30.737
For a single run, I can choose

00:30.737 --> 00:33.047
a different limit on the command line.

00:33.047 --> 00:35.356
Here I ask Deslop to report without

00:35.356 --> 00:37.666
failing because of repeated code. This changes

00:37.666 --> 00:39.976
the check for this run, without rewriting

00:39.976 --> 00:41.956
the settings the team has saved.

00:42.756 --> 00:45.070
Now I set a five-percent limit as

00:45.070 --> 00:47.384
an example and run the check again.

00:47.384 --> 00:49.697
This project is over that limit, so

00:49.697 --> 00:52.011
the command fails and still writes its

00:52.011 --> 00:54.324
report. I inspect the result to see

00:54.324 --> 00:56.307
which repeated code caused the failure.
